<title>GERMANY: Conti considers closing a European plant.</title>
<headline>Conti considers closing a European plant.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tyre manufacturer Continental AG on Tuesday said it would step up restructuring efforts and may close one of its three European commercial tyre plants if sales did not improve.</p>
<p>The group, which employs 46,400 people around the world, also said it would cut its workforce by at least 1,400 jobs, in part as it begins this year to implement a new manufacturing process expected to slash inventory and overhead costs.</p>
<p>Continental said 1997 first quarter pre-tax earnings rose to 88 million marks compared with 75 million marks in the 1996 first quarter behind a 1.4 percent rise in global sales to 2.52 billion marks for the three-month period.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
